{"tool_name":"amplify","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"amplify","home":"https://github.com/bcgsc/AMPlify","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"AMPlify is an attentive deep learning model for antimicrobial peptide prediction.","addition_date":"2022-06-08T09:12:25.699422Z","last_update_date":"2022-06-08T09:12:25.701972Z","tool_type":["Workflow"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:amplify","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"ibirol@bcgsc.ca","name":"Inanc Birol","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0950-7839","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Antimicrobial resistance prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3482"},{"term":"Sequence trimming","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3192"},{"term":"Virulence prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3461"}]}],"name":"AMPlify","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Chan019","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/S12864-022-08310-4","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2022, The Author(s).Background: Antibiotic resistance is a growing global health concern prompting researchers to seek alternatives to conventional antibiotics. Antimicrobial peptides (AMPs) are attracting attention again as therapeutic agents with promising utility in this domain, and using in silico methods to discover novel AMPs is a strategy that is gaining interest. Such methods can sift through large volumes of candidate sequences and reduce lab screening costs. Results: Here we introduce AMPlify, an attentive deep learning model for AMP prediction, and demonstrate its utility in prioritizing peptide sequences derived from the Rana [Lithobates] catesbeiana (bullfrog) genome. We tested the bioactivity of our predicted peptides against a panel of bacterial species, including representatives from the World Health Organization\u2019s priority pathogens list. Four of our novel AMPs were active against multiple species of bacteria, including a multi-drug resistant isolate of carbapenemase-producing Escherichia coli. Conclusions: We demonstrate the utility of deep learning based tools like AMPlify in our fight against antibiotic resistance. We expect such tools to play a significant role in discovering novel candidates of peptide-based alternatives to classical antibiotics.","authors":[{"name":"Bergman L."},{"name":"Birol I."},{"name":"Cameron C.E."},{"name":"Hammond S.A."},{"name":"Helbing C.C."},{"name":"Hoang L.M.N."},{"name":"Houston S."},{"name":"Li C."},{"name":"Sutherland D."},{"name":"Taho F."},{"name":"Warren R.L."},{"name":"Wong T."},{"name":"Yang C."}],"citationCount":3,"date":"2022-12-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"BMC Genomics","title":"AMPlify: attentive deep learning model for discovery of novel antimicrobial peptides effective against WHO priority pathogens"},"pmcid":"PMC8788131","pmid":"35078402"}],"topic":[{"term":"Machine learning","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3474"},{"term":"Sequencing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3168"},{"term":"Small molecules","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0154"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"AMPlify","home":"https://bio.tools/amplify","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"AMPlify is an attentive deep learning model for antimicrobial peptide prediction.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:amplify/workflow/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":true,"registration":false},"packages":true,"source_packages":true,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":true,"license":true,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":117,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2020"},